### AML demo (FR-AML-2 R2 "structuring" -> FR-AML-3 freeze). LOCAL ONLY, Razorpay TEST MODE, fake users only.
# Walkthrough with SQL and Kafka commands: docs/aml-demo.md. Run the requests top to bottom.
# Prerequisites:
#   - core-app (8080) and risk-aml-service (8081) running with the local profile, infra from compose;
#   - customer1 at FULL KYC (kyc.http), customer2 with at least a MIN wallet (auth.http "minimum KYC" as customer2);
#   - environment "local" selected, password in http-client.private.env.json (see auth.http).
# Tokens live 5 minutes: if a request says 401, run the token requests again.

@token_url = {{keycloak}}/realms/{{realm}}/protocol/openid-connect/token
# officer1 needs a fresh TOTP code: Git Bash, from dev/:  scripts/aml-demo-webhooks.sh totp
@otp = 000000

### 1. customer1: token
POST {{token_url}}
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=password&client_id=trustledger-dev&username=customer1&password={{password}}

> {% client.global.set("customer1_token", response.body.access_token); %}

### 2. customer2: token
POST {{token_url}}
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=password&client_id=trustledger-dev&username=customer2&password={{password}}

> {% client.global.set("customer2_token", response.body.access_token); %}

### 3. customer1: wallet -> 200 {tier FULL, status ACTIVE}; FULL allows ₹2,00,000 a month, enough for 3 x ₹46,000
GET {{api}}/api/v1/wallets/me
Authorization: Bearer {{customer1_token}}

> {% client.global.set("sender_wallet_id", response.body.walletId); %}

### 4. customer2: wallet (recipient of the transfer in step 9)
GET {{api}}/api/v1/wallets/me
Authorization: Bearer {{customer2_token}}

> {% client.global.set("receiver_wallet_id", response.body.walletId); %}

### 5a. customer1: top-up 1 of ₹46,000 -> 201 PENDING (inside R2's ₹45,000-₹49,999.99 band)
# The Idempotency-Key makes a rerun return the SAME top-up. For a second demo run, generate new keys:
# {{$random.uuid}} does that, but then a rerun creates a new top-up every time.
POST {{api}}/api/v1/topups
Authorization: Bearer {{customer1_token}}
Idempotency-Key: {{$random.uuid}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"amount": "46000.00"}

> {% client.global.set("topup1", response.body.id); %}

### 5b. customer1: top-up 2 of ₹46,000 -> 201 PENDING
POST {{api}}/api/v1/topups
Authorization: Bearer {{customer1_token}}
Idempotency-Key: {{$random.uuid}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"amount": "46000.00"}

> {% client.global.set("topup2", response.body.id); %}

### 5c. customer1: top-up 3 of ₹46,000 -> 201 PENDING
POST {{api}}/api/v1/topups
Authorization: Bearer {{customer1_token}}
Idempotency-Key: {{$random.uuid}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"amount": "46000.00"}

> {%
  client.global.set("topup3", response.body.id);
  client.log("Pay them (docs/aml-demo.md step 4). Fast way, Git Bash in dev/:");
  client.log("scripts/aml-demo-webhooks.sh capture " + client.global.get("topup1") + " "
      + client.global.get("topup2") + " " + response.body.id);
%}

### 6. STOP: pay the three top-ups now (docs/aml-demo.md step 4: checkout.html, or the webhook script).
# Then: each top-up -> 200 CAPTURED
GET {{api}}/api/v1/topups/{{topup3}}
Authorization: Bearer {{customer1_token}}

### 7. customer1: wallet a few seconds after the third capture -> 200 {status FROZEN, balance "138000.00"}
# (outbox -> Kafka -> AML rule R2 -> aml.freeze_requests -> relay -> Kafka -> core-app freeze; about 1-3 s)
GET {{api}}/api/v1/wallets/me
Authorization: Bearer {{customer1_token}}

### 8. A fourth top-up while frozen -> 409 WALLET_FROZEN (no Razorpay order is created)
POST {{api}}/api/v1/topups
Authorization: Bearer {{customer1_token}}
Idempotency-Key: {{$random.uuid}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"amount": "100.00"}

### 9. THE POINT OF THE DEMO: customer1 -> customer2 ₹100 -> 409 ProblemDetail {code WALLET_FROZEN}
POST {{api}}/api/v1/transfers
Authorization: Bearer {{customer1_token}}
Idempotency-Key: {{$random.uuid}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"recipientWalletId": "{{receiver_wallet_id}}", "amount": "100.00", "note": "AML demo"}

### --- The compliance side (risk-aml-service, port 8081) ---

### 10. officer1: token (paste a fresh code into @otp first; valid 30 s, one login per code)
POST {{token_url}}
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=password&client_id=trustledger-dev&username=officer1&password={{password}}&totp={{otp}}

> {% client.global.set("officer1_token", response.body.access_token); %}

### 11. officer1: open cases for customer1's wallet -> 200 {content: [{status OPEN, highestSeverity HIGH}]}
GET {{aml}}/api/v1/aml/cases?status=OPEN&walletId={{sender_wallet_id}}&page=0&size=20
Authorization: Bearer {{officer1_token}}

> {% client.global.set("aml_case_id", response.body.content[0].id); %}

### 12. officer1: the case -> 200 {alerts [R2 HIGH], freezeRequests [{publishedAt set}], facts [3 x IN 46000.00]}
GET {{aml}}/api/v1/aml/cases/{{aml_case_id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{officer1_token}}

### 13. STR export before escalation -> 409 INVALID_STATE_TRANSITION (only ESCALATED cases have a report)
GET {{aml}}/api/v1/aml/cases/{{aml_case_id}}/str-report
Authorization: Bearer {{officer1_token}}

### 14. officer1: assign to self (empty body) -> 200 INVESTIGATING
POST {{aml}}/api/v1/aml/cases/{{aml_case_id}}/assign
Authorization: Bearer {{officer1_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### 15. officer1: escalate -> 200 ESCALATED (closing as FALSE_POSITIVE would NOT unfreeze the wallet)
POST {{aml}}/api/v1/aml/cases/{{aml_case_id}}/escalate
Authorization: Bearer {{officer1_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"notes": "Three top-ups of 46,000 in one day, just under the 50,000 hold. Filing an STR."}

### 16. officer1: STR report -> 200 text/csv, attachment; wallet and officer IDs masked to ****last4
GET {{aml}}/api/v1/aml/cases/{{aml_case_id}}/str-report
Authorization: Bearer {{officer1_token}}

### 17. A customer on the AML API -> 403
GET {{aml}}/api/v1/aml/cases
Authorization: Bearer {{customer1_token}}
